    {
      "id": "claim_77e13900a43d4b17b8fff09bc15119c5",
      "statement": "Agent tool side effects are step-transactional: all agent-authored code changes buffer in memory until the step's persistence barrier, where one transaction persists the step's message, appends the buffered rows, materializes the single changes message, retires the rows, and stamps pending gadget/binding records — agent rows are born and retired in the same transaction, and a step that dies before its barrier leaves only an unstamped registry record that reconcilePendingGadgets reaps.",
